  },
  "description": "HANWIF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C193 H260 Cr1 Dy6 N5 O30,7(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 17 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.123-4.930 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.52-166.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C200H288CrDy6N5O37. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
